1jda|v|Having the power to give form or fashion to a mass of matter; as, the plastic hand of the Creator. ; Capable of being molded, formed, or modeled, as clay or plaster; -- used also figuratively; as, the plastic mind of a child. ; Pertaining or appropriate to, or characteristic of, molding or modeling; produced by, or appearing as if produced by, molding or modeling; -- said of sculpture and the kindred arts, in distinction from painting and the graphic arts.	o:244v,16,1~244v,16,1
