1je2|n|A plat; a plan; a sketch; a model; a pattern. Used also figuratively. ; A place laid out after a model. ; Any flat or horizontal surface; especially, one that is raised above some particular level, as a framework of timber or boards horizontally joined so as to form a roof, or a raised floor, or portion of a floor; a landing; a dais; a stage, for speakers, performers, or workmen; a standing place. ; A declaration of the principles upon which a person, a sect, or a party proposes to stand; a declared policy or system; as, the Saybrook platform; a political platform. ; A light deck, usually placed in a section of the hold or over the floor of the magazine. See Orlop.	a:25i3,74,3;daq,59,4;9jl,51,24;gtg,36,1;vrg,21,5;1cf9,17,2;1uus,16,3;1urr,16,5;e4r,15,1;1e3p,15,4~9jl,51,24;1urr,16,5;vrg,21,5;7c0,13,5;1ru6,2,5;daq,59,4;1e3p,15,4;1wir,3,3;1uus,16,3;25i3,74,3	v:1b59,34,4;x3x,33,3;15kd,21,5;1lmu,16,5~15kd,21,5;1lmu,16,5;1b59,34,4;x3x,33,3	n:gtg,52,3;18lg,44,5;daq,39,1;9jo,33,2;1mob,26,5;e4r,25,2;a7o,22,2;28hy,17,2;1ytq,16,2;1lmq,14,6~1lmq,14,6;1mob,26,5;18lg,44,5;29d3,6,3;1lmu,8,3;6r5,8,3;gtg,52,3;e4r,25,2;a7o,22,2;28hy,17,2	N:1b56,28,1;1v0x,23,2;zf8,7,3~zf8,7,3;1v0x,23,2;1b56,28,1
