1jh5|a|To give pleasure to; to excite agreeable sensations or emotions in; to make glad; to gratify; to content; to satisfy. ; To have or take pleasure in; hence, to choose; to wish; to desire; to will. ; To be the will or pleasure of; to seem good to; -- used impersonally. ; To afford or impart pleasure; to excite agreeable emotions. ; To have pleasure; to be willing, as a matter of affording pleasure or showing favor; to vouchsafe; to consent.	j:1ptz,25,5;6o8,23,4;l8n,16,1;1p20,7,1;27rw,4,5;1qaq,4,1~27rw,4,5;1ptz,25,5;6o8,23,4;1qaq,4,1;l8n,16,1;1p20,7,1
